(Was: stage 1e2 cycle/depth safety, pinning `set m's "self" to m` as a
 genuine self-referential cycle truncated by the shared 64-deep
 `_print_depth` budget. docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #111 (owner ruling, GitHub #34,
 Option 1): a collection placed inside another collection is now a COPY,
 so this copies m's state at the moment of the `set` (here, `{"a": 1}`,
 no "self" key yet) and stores that copy under "self" - it can no longer
 construct a real cycle. `m` ends up one level deep, not infinite.)

a map called m is {"a": 1}.
set m's "self" to m.
print m.
on error print "truncated".
